segments.text:
Some think the Martyrs were too prodigall of their bloud, and that they might have beene better advised; but such are unacquainted with the force of the love of God kindled in the heart of his childe, which makes him set such a high price upon Christ and his truth, that he counts not his life dear unto him;
He knowes hee is not his owne, but hath given up himselfe to Christ, and therefore all that is his, yea if hee had more lives to give for Christ, hee should have them. He knowes he shall be no looser by it. Hee knowes it is not a
losse of his life, but an exchange for a better.
